units('b279',r'''
蜿蜒度與量測尺度~Sinuosity and measurement scale || 蜿蜒度比較沿河道中心線與谷地參考路徑的長度，能描述平面幾何，卻不直接代表棲地品質或洪水安全。中心線取自低水槽、滿岸線或影像水面時可能得到不同結果，谷地長度也必須固定相同起訖點。影像解析度太細會把小幅岸線起伏計入長度，太粗則削去彎道。因此工程前後比較應維持相同定義與解析度，先確認幾何變化是真實河道重組而非測圖方式改變。~Sinuosity compares channel-centreline length with a valley reference route, describing plan geometry rather than habitat quality or flood safety. A centreline based on low flow, bankfull edges or visible water can differ, and valley length must use matching endpoints. Fine imagery may count minor irregularities while coarse mapping removes bends. Keep definitions and resolution consistent before and after works so an apparent change represents channel reorganization rather than a different surveying method or mapping scale. || Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless || 相同起訖點與固定中心線定義，只描述平面長度比~Matching endpoints and a fixed centreline definition; describes plan-length ratio only || 使用同一底圖投影及解析度數化工程前後中心線，保留起訖點和谷地基準路徑。以第二位判讀者重畫部分彎道估計主觀差異，再將長度改變與實際開挖或自然遷移位置核對，避免把繪圖密度當成果。~Digitize both centrelines using the same projection and resolution, preserving endpoints and valley reference. Have another interpreter redraw selected bends to estimate subjective variation, then compare length changes with actual excavation or migration rather than treating denser digitizing as improvement. || 不同年份使用不同解析度影像可能製造虛假蜿蜒度增加，洪水影像還可能把漫流支線誤認主槽。診斷應先檢查中心線定義及流量條件。~Different image resolutions can create false sinuosity gains, while flood imagery may confuse overbank branches with the main channel. Check centreline definitions and flow conditions before interpreting apparent geometric improvement. || 蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好~Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect || 在谷地長度固定下將河長增加一成重算蜿蜒度，另畫一個增加長度但缺少洪氾空間的方案。說明還需哪些水理及生態證據才能比較兩者。~Increase channel length by ten percent at fixed valley length and recalculate sinuosity. Sketch a longer channel without additional floodplain space, then identify hydraulic and ecological evidence needed to compare the alternatives. || 1800/1200 || 1.5 || dimensionless || .000001
展長後的平均坡度~Mean slope after lengthening || 在上游與下游控制高程不變時，河道展長會降低沿程平均坡度，但各彎段的床坡不必均勻。局部深潭、淺瀨與回水可能分配大部分水頭損失，因此不能把平均坡度直接視為每一點能坡。坡度降低也會改變輸砂能力，若上游供砂維持不變，河床可能淤積再調整。設計應把高程控制、幾何長度與預期泥砂交換連在一起，而非只透過平面曲線追求更大的蜿蜒度。~With fixed upstream and downstream control elevations, channel lengthening reduces mean longitudinal slope, but individual bends need not share that slope. Pools, riffles and backwater distribute losses unevenly, so mean bed slope is not the energy slope everywhere. Lower slope can alter transport capacity and trigger deposition when upstream sediment supply persists. Connect elevation controls, channel geometry and sediment exchange rather than pursuing a larger sinuosity value through planform geometry alone without checking adjustment. || dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless || 固定兩端床高的平均幾何坡度，不代替局部能坡或輸砂平衡~Mean geometric slope at fixed endpoint bed levels, not local energy slope or sediment equilibrium || 重測兩端控制高程與沿程縱斷面，將深潭、淺瀨及構造物逐一標示。另量代表流量下水面坡度，對照床坡差異；若出現大範圍回水，應調查下游控制而非把所有差異歸因於新彎道。~Survey endpoint controls and the full profile, identifying pools, riffles and structures. Measure water-surface slope at representative discharge and compare with bed slope. Extensive backwater requires investigating downstream control instead of attributing every difference to the new bends. || 若只增加河長卻忽略下游固定水位，上游可能產生預期外壅水。床面局部淤積也可能重新縮短有效流路，需追蹤水面與地形的共同演變。~Lengthening while ignoring a fixed downstream level can create unexpected upstream backwater. Local deposition may also shorten the effective flow path, requiring joint monitoring of water levels and evolving channel geometry. || 河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度~Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge || 將河長縮短三百公尺重算平均坡度，保持兩端高程不變。畫出兩個具有相同平均坡但局部深潭配置不同的縱斷面，說明其水理仍可能不同。~Shorten the channel by three hundred metres with endpoint levels fixed and recalculate slope. Draw two profiles with identical mean slope but different pool distributions, explaining why their hydraulic behaviour may still differ. || 3/1800 || .001666667 || dimensionless || .000000001
粗糙度與通水尺度~Roughness and conveyance scale || 復育後植生、木構與河床形態會改變阻力，用曼寧式可初步比較斷面通水尺度，但必須確認近似均勻流及適用的單位系統。粗糙係數不是純粹材料常數，會隨淹水深度、植生彎伏和季節改變。複式斷面中主槽與洪氾地的交換也難由單一係數描述。計算應保留面積、水力半徑與能坡各自來源，不可用調整係數掩蓋幾何或邊界條件的錯誤。~Restored vegetation, wood and bed forms change resistance. Manning's relation offers a preliminary conveyance comparison under approximately uniform flow and a stated unit system. Roughness is not merely a material constant; depth, plant reconfiguration and season affect it. Exchange between the main channel and floodplain also exceeds a single-coefficient description. Keep the origins of area, hydraulic radius and energy slope explicit instead of tuning roughness to conceal errors in geometry or boundary conditions. || n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s || SI 曼寧形式的近均勻流示例，能坡為獨立假設且非前單元床坡~SI Manning approximation for near-uniform flow; energy slope is independently assumed, not the preceding unit's bed slope || 對數個流量實測水位與速度，先驗證斷面幾何，再比較推算係數是否隨水深系統性改變。分別調查有葉與落葉狀態，若主槽和洪氾地速度差很大，應分區估算並考慮側向交換。~Measure levels and velocities at several discharges, verify geometry first, and check systematic depth dependence in inferred roughness. Survey leafy and leafless conditions separately. Strong main-channel and floodplain velocity contrasts call for divided treatment and attention to lateral exchange. || 用低水位校準的粗糙係數外推洪水，可能誤估植生淹沒後阻力或洪氾通道。若模擬僅在某一水深吻合，應查機制而非宣稱全流量範圍已驗證。~Roughness calibrated at low flow can misrepresent submerged vegetation and floodplain pathways during floods. Agreement at one depth does not validate the full discharge range; investigate the changing resistance mechanism before extrapolation. || 曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變~Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth || 將粗糙係數增加四分之一並保持幾何與能坡不變，重算通水量。說明真實河道為何可能改以水位上升回應，並列出判斷所需的邊界條件。~Increase roughness by one quarter at fixed geometry and energy slope and recompute discharge. Explain why a real river may instead respond through rising stage, identifying boundary conditions needed to distinguish these responses. || 24*1.2**(2/3)*math.sqrt(.0015)/.04 || 26.241241 || m3/s || .000001
洪氾地的可用蓄水~Available floodplain storage || 重新連接洪氾地可增加水體暫存空間，但蓄水量取決於地形、水位與進出水時間，而非整片土地面積。以平均淹水深乘面積只是給定水位下的幾何容量，若入口太窄或洪峰太短，空間可能來不及填滿。原本已積水的窪地還需扣除既有水量。削峰效果則取決於容量何時使用與何時退水，必須把容量和流量歷線一起分析，不能把立方公尺直接說成洪峰降低值。~Reconnecting a floodplain creates potential temporary storage, but usable volume depends on topography, stage and exchange timing rather than land area alone. Area times mean depth gives geometric capacity at a specified stage; a narrow entrance or brief peak may prevent filling. Existing ponded water reduces available capacity. Peak attenuation also depends on filling and drainage timing, so evaluate storage alongside hydrographs instead of treating a volume as if it were a discharge reduction. || A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3 || 指定水位下新增平均水深且無既存積水，不推算洪峰削減~Added mean depth at a specified stage with no pre-existing water; peak reduction is not inferred || 以地形模型建立水位容量關係，現場核對低窪與阻水土堤。洪水時同步量入口、出口流量及洪氾水位，檢查容量是否真正利用，並比較退水時序，避免只用最高水痕估算整段防洪作用。~Develop a stage-storage relation from terrain and verify depressions and embankments. During events, synchronize inlet and outlet flows with floodplain levels to determine actual use and drainage timing, rather than inferring flood protection solely from the highest water mark. || 洪氾入口堵塞可能使圖上容量無法使用，出口過快又可能把水送回洪峰。應檢查連通與時間，而非只增加名義土地面積。~A blocked entrance can make mapped storage inaccessible, while rapid drainage can return water during the peak. Investigate connectivity and timing rather than assuming more nominal floodplain area will necessarily improve attenuation. || 幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量~Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge || 假設事件前已有十公分積水，重算剩餘容量。畫出提早及延後填水兩種歷線，說明即使使用相同體積，對下游洪峰仍可能產生不同影響。~Assume ten centimetres of water is already present and recalculate remaining capacity. Draw early and late filling hydrographs and explain why equal stored volumes can have different effects on the downstream peak. || 60000*.35 || 21000 || m3 || .000001
彎道橫向水面差~Transverse water level in bends || 水流轉彎需要向心加速度，橫向水面坡度可提供相應壓力差，因此外彎水面可能較高。簡化關係以平均速度、河寬和曲率半徑建立尺度，但真實彎道還有二次流、深槽及垂直速度分布。外彎侵蝕並不只由水面高差決定，近床流向與土體條件同樣重要。再蜿蜒設計應把曲率、岸趾及洪氾邊界一起檢查，避免把平面美觀的急彎當成自然穩定形狀。~Turning flow requires centripetal acceleration, which a transverse water-surface gradient can help supply, producing higher levels near the outer bend. A simplified relation uses mean velocity, width and curvature radius, while real bends include secondary circulation, thalweg variation and vertical velocity structure. Outer-bank erosion is not determined by surface difference alone; near-bed currents and soil matter. Examine curvature, toe conditions and floodplain boundaries together rather than assuming an attractive planform is naturally stable. || v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m || 小寬徑比與代表平均速度的尺度估算，未解析二次流~Scale estimate using modest width-to-radius ratio and representative mean velocity, without resolving secondary circulation || 在同一斷面同步量內外彎水位，並取得垂向與橫向流速資料。量測曲率時保持中心線定義一致，若水面差與簡式偏離，先查回水、非均勻速度及幾何急變，不把偏差全歸為測量誤差。~Measure inner and outer levels simultaneously and obtain vertical and transverse velocity data. Use a consistent centreline for curvature. Differences from the simple estimate require checking backwater, nonuniform velocity and abrupt geometry before attributing everything to survey error. || 急彎可能把主流壓向尚未穩定的外岸，造成局部淘空和岸塊崩落。即使橫向水面差不大，也不能排除近床高速或土體弱面。~A tight bend can direct the main current toward an unestablished outer bank, causing undermining and block failure. Modest surface difference does not rule out fast near-bed flow or weak soil layers. || 橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷~A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode || 將曲率半徑縮小一半而速度與河寬固定，重算水面差。畫出可能的二次流方向並說明簡式沒有提供哪些近床資訊，安排相應測速位置。~Halve curvature radius at fixed speed and width and recalculate level difference. Sketch possible secondary circulation, identify near-bed information missing from the formula, and place velocity measurements to investigate those processes. || 1.5**2*12/(9.81*60) || .045872 || m || .000001
岸線遷移與土方體積~Bank migration and eroded volume || 允許河道在限定走廊內遷移，可以提供沉積物和新生棲地，但也需要清楚界定土地、設施與管理邊界。岸線後退距離乘長度與平均高度，可初估流失土體的原位體積，並非全部會立即成為下游懸浮泥砂。崩落土塊可能暫存岸趾、再被洪水分次帶走，細粗料行為也不同。監測應區分平面遷移、體積侵蝕與輸出通量，避免把三個量互相代替。~Allowing migration within a defined corridor can create habitat and supply sediment, but land, infrastructure and management boundaries must be explicit. Retreat distance times bank length and mean height estimates in-place eroded volume, not sediment immediately exported downstream. Failed blocks may remain at the toe and be removed during later floods, with fines and coarse material behaving differently. Monitor planform movement, volumetric erosion and exported flux separately rather than substituting one quantity for another. || L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place || 均勻矩形岸塊幾何估算，未轉成固體質量或下游輸砂量~Uniform rectangular bank-block estimate, not converted to solid mass or downstream sediment export || 用相同高程與平面基準比較岸頂、岸趾及水下地形，量崩落塊體是否仍留在控制體內。若需換算質量，另採原位密度與含水資料；再用下游採樣判斷何時輸出，避免把體積直接當通量。~Compare bank crest, toe and submerged terrain on common datums and measure failed blocks remaining inside the control volume. Mass conversion needs density and moisture data; downstream sampling identifies export timing instead of treating volume as a transport rate. || 僅用岸頂退縮會漏掉水下掏空，也可能把斜坡整形當成天然侵蝕。若忽略暫存崩塊，下游輸砂模型會過早加入全部土方而誇大峰值。~Crest retreat alone can miss underwater undercutting or confuse grading with natural erosion. Ignoring stored blocks also injects all eroded material into a transport model too early and exaggerates downstream sediment peaks. || 岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面~All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment || 將平均岸高增加三分之一重算體積，再假設一半崩塊暫留岸趾，列出剩餘輸出上限與所需證據。說明為何這仍不是完整輸砂歷線。~Increase mean bank height by one third and recalculate volume. Assume half remains at the toe, describe the remaining export bound and required evidence, and explain why this still does not provide a transport hydrograph. || 240*2.5*1.8 || 1080 || m3 || .000001
側汊連通的交換水量~Exchange volume through a side channel || 再連接側汊可改變主槽與洪氾地的水量、泥砂和生物交換，但流向可能隨主河水位升降而反轉。流量乘時間只適用於已知定常流段，變動事件需要逐時積分並保留正負號。流入量不等同淨蓄水，若另一出口同時排出，水體只是通過。設計應把入口、出口與內部水位畫成控制體，並關注過低水位時是否形成孤立水塘或阻斷生物退路。~Reconnecting a side channel changes water, sediment and biological exchange with the main river, but direction can reverse as river stage rises and falls. Discharge times duration applies to a known steady interval; variable events require signed integration. Inflow is not net storage when another outlet simultaneously drains the area. Draw inlet, outlet and internal water levels as a control volume and examine whether low stages isolate pools or interrupt return routes for organisms. || Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3 || 定常向內流量之總流入體積，不等於淨蓄水或削峰量~Gross inflow volume during steady inward flow, not net storage or peak attenuation || 同步量側汊入口及出口的水位與流量，採可辨方向的儀器並統一正號。將流量積分與水位容量變化比較，檢查地下滲漏或未量支路；退水期另追蹤斷流位置，確認連通性不是只有洪峰時存在。~Measure inlet and outlet levels and signed flows simultaneously. Compare integrated exchange with stage-storage change and investigate seepage or unmeasured branches. During recession, track where flow disconnects so connectivity is not assessed solely at the flood peak. || 出口未量而只記入口流量，會高估側汊蓄水效益；退水時若形成孤立池，還可能把先前進入的生物困住。需連續追蹤整個水位循環。~Recording only inlet flow exaggerates storage when an unmeasured outlet is active. Disconnected recession pools can also trap organisms that entered earlier, requiring observation across the complete stage cycle rather than only rising water. || 側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積~Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume || 加入每秒零點三立方公尺的同時出流，重算兩小時淨蓄水。再畫流向反轉的退水階段，指出積分正負號與生物退路各需如何檢查。~Add simultaneous outflow of zero point three cubic metres per second and compute net storage over two hours. Sketch reversal during recession and explain checks for both integration signs and organism return routes. || .8*7200 || 5760 || m3 || .000001
河岸地下水交換~Groundwater exchange across banks || 河道復育改變水位與流路後，地下水可能向河道補注，也可能由河道暫時滲入岸土。達西式用水頭梯度與滲透係數估算體積通量，適用於已定義的飽和多孔介質控制面。孔隙中的平均實際流速還需要除有效孔隙率，不能把達西通量直接當成示蹤旅行速度。層狀沉積物可能有方向性，河床堵塞也會改變交換，所以監測須同時掌握水頭、介質與水質。~Restoration can shift groundwater discharge to the river or drive temporary bank infiltration. Darcy's relation estimates volume flux from conductivity and head gradient across a defined saturated porous section. Average pore-water velocity additionally depends on effective porosity; Darcy flux is not directly tracer travel speed. Layering can create directional conductivity, and bed clogging can alter exchange. Monitor heads, sediment properties and water quality together to distinguish changes in hydraulic connection from changes in the source water. || K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s || 飽和均質一維定常達西流，水頭差方向已指定~Saturated homogeneous one-dimensional steady Darcy flow with a specified head-gradient direction || 在河道與岸內井使用同一高程基準量水頭，透過適合土層的試驗估滲透係數。以溫度或保守示蹤資料比對交換方向，若水頭響應有明顯延遲，應加入儲水與非定常效應而非維持定常假設。~Measure river and well heads on the same datum and estimate conductivity with tests appropriate to the strata. Compare exchange direction using temperature or conservative tracers. Delayed head responses require storage and transient effects instead of retaining a steady-flow assumption. || 以表層砂樣代表深部黏土夾層會高估交換量，堵塞層形成後原係數也可能失效。若模型流量大但示蹤反應弱，應查層理與有效連通面積。~Using surface sand to represent a deeper clay layer exaggerates exchange, and new clogging can invalidate earlier conductivity estimates. Large modeled flux with weak tracer response warrants checking layering and the effectively connected area. || 達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度~Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores || 將水頭差反向而大小不變，計算帶符號流量並畫交換方向。另指定有效孔隙率，說明由通量換算孔隙速度還需要哪個面積定義與流路假設。~Reverse the head difference without changing magnitude and calculate signed discharge. Specify an effective porosity and explain the area definition and pathway assumptions needed to convert Darcy flux into average pore velocity. || .00002*300*.4/20 || .00012 || m3/s || .000000001
水體平移與洪波傳播~Water advection and flood-wave travel || 河道延長可能增加水體沿流路的平移時間，但洪波傳播速度並不等於水粒子平均流速。以長度除速度得到的是固定速度的平流尺度，未計彌散、死水交換或水位波形變化。示蹤物可能早到也可能留下長尾，洪峰則受蓄水及邊界影響。評估復育的時間效益時，應分別量測示蹤突破、洪水歷線與局部流速，避免用水的旅行時間直接宣稱下游洪峰必然延後同樣秒數。~Lengthening can increase water-parcel advection time, but flood-wave celerity differs from mean parcel velocity. Length divided by velocity gives a constant-speed advection scale without dispersion, inactive-zone exchange or changing wave shape. Tracers can arrive early and leave long tails, while flood peaks depend on storage and boundaries. Evaluate tracer breakthrough, hydrographs and local velocity separately rather than claiming downstream peak delay directly from the calculated travel time of water parcels through the restored reach. || L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s || 定常均速平流時間尺度，不是洪峰傳播或完整示蹤停留分布~Steady uniform advection scale, not flood-peak travel or a full tracer residence distribution || 在合法且適合的示蹤試驗中量測上下游濃度曲線，另用同步水位流量觀測洪波。比較首達、質心與峰值時間，並說明各自物理意義；若差異大，檢查死水交換及沿程支流，不能任選最有利數字。~Use an appropriate authorized tracer test for concentration histories and synchronized level-discharge observations for flood waves. Compare first arrival, centroid and peak times with their distinct meanings. Large differences warrant checking inactive-zone exchange and tributaries rather than selecting a favourable statistic. || 把示蹤質心時間當洪峰延遲，可能誇大防洪效果；相反地，忽略長尾也會低估污染物停留。應根據問題選指標，避免混用不同時間尺度。~Using tracer-centroid travel as flood-peak delay can exaggerate protection, while ignoring long tails understates contaminant persistence. Choose the time metric for the actual question instead of mixing different transport and wave processes. || 水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間~Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream || 將平均流速降低兩成重算平流時間，再畫一條有長尾的示蹤曲線及一條洪水歷線。標出不能直接互換的時間，列出檢驗削峰所需額外資料。~Reduce mean velocity by twenty percent and recalculate advection time. Draw a long-tailed tracer curve and a flood hydrograph, label noninterchangeable times, and identify additional evidence needed to evaluate peak attenuation. || 1800/.6 || 3000 || s || .000001
地形差分的量測不確定性~Uncertainty in terrain differences || 工程前後地形差分可找出沖淤，但小變化可能只是測量誤差。兩期獨立隨機高程誤差的標準差可用平方和開根號合成，若兩期共享基準偏差或植生遮蔽，獨立假設便不成立。單點標準差也不等於整個土方體積的誤差，空間相關會改變總量不確定性。分析應先分離系統偏差與隨機分散，再清楚報告檢出尺度，而不把所有不同顏色像元當成真實侵蝕或沉積。~Terrain differencing reveals erosion and deposition, but small changes may be survey noise. Independent random elevation standard deviations combine by root sum of squares; shared datum errors or vegetation bias violate independence. Point uncertainty also differs from volume uncertainty because spatial correlation affects aggregation. Separate systematic bias from random scatter and state the detection scale clearly, rather than interpreting every coloured difference pixel as real morphological change or assigning confidence without an explicit error model. || s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m || 兩期獨立零均值隨機誤差的差分標準差，非自動的可信界限~Difference standard deviation for independent zero-mean random errors, not an automatic confidence bound || 在穩定未變區檢查兩期高程偏差，先校正可識別系統差，再分析殘差分布與空間相關。用獨立控制點驗證，並分別報裸地與植生區精度；設定檢出門檻時需交代誤差分布及採用的信心水準。~Check differences on stable ground, correct identifiable systematic shifts, and examine residual distributions and spatial correlation. Validate with independent control points and separate bare-ground from vegetated accuracy. Any detection threshold needs a stated error distribution and confidence level. || 未校正的共同高程偏移會讓整段河道看似淤積或侵蝕，植生高度也可能被當成地面。若差分呈現整區同號，應先查基準及分類再解釋地形過程。~An uncorrected datum shift can make the whole reach appear to deposit or erode, and vegetation may be mistaken for ground. Region-wide differences of one sign call for checking datum and classification before interpreting geomorphic processes. || 兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化~Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change || 假設第二期標準差降到兩公分，重算差分精度並比較改善幅度。再提出兩期誤差相關的情況，說明為何不能繼續使用獨立平方和公式宣稱同樣精度。~Reduce the second survey standard deviation to two centimetres and recompute difference uncertainty. Describe a source of correlated errors and explain why the independent root-sum-square formula would then require modification before claiming equivalent accuracy. || math.sqrt(.03**2+.04**2) || .05 || m || .000001
''')
